# Model separation and data flow

Typical flow: **HTTP request** → (optional) **API request** + **AutoMapper** → **MediatR command/query** → **handler** → **repository / entity** → **DTO** → **AutoMapper** → **API response** → JSON.

| Type | Location | Purpose |
|------|----------|---------|
| **Entity** | `backend/MotoklubBezbednost.Data/Models/*.cs` | EF Core persistence model |
| **DTO** | `backend/MotoklubBezbednost.Business/Dtos/*.cs` | Shapes returned to the API / used between handlers |
| **Command / Query** | `backend/MotoklubBezbednost.Business/Cqrs/**/Commands|Queries/*.cs` | MediatR messages |
| **Handler** | `backend/MotoklubBezbednost.Business/Cqrs/**/Handlers/*.cs` | Orchestration, validation, mapping entity ↔ DTO |
| **API request** | `backend/MotoklubBezbednost.API/Models/Requests/**/*.cs` | Incoming payloads when not bound as primitives only |
| **API response** | `backend/MotoklubBezbednost.API/Models/Responses/*.cs` | HTTP response shapes (map from Business DTOs at the controller) |
| **AutoMapper profiles** | `backend/MotoklubBezbednost.API/Mappings/ApiMappingProfile.cs`, `backend/MotoklubBezbednost.Business/Mappings/BusinessMappingProfile.cs` | API: request ↔ CQRS, DTO ↔ response; Business: entity ↔ DTO, create/update commands ↔ entity |

- Keep **entities** out of API contracts; expose **response models** (or DTOs only inside Business).
- Keep **API mapping vs Business mapping** in separate profiles/assemblies; register both from `Program.cs`.
